DEADLOCK is a situation where 2 or more threads are blocked forever, waiting for each other to release a resource.
This typically occurs when 2 or more threads have a circular dependencies on a set of lock.

DEADLOCK CONDITIONS

1. Mutual exclusion: One thread can access a resource at a time.

2. Hold and Wait: A thread holding at least one resource is waiting to acquire additional resources held by other threads.

3. No preemption: Resources cannot be forcibly taken from thread holding them.

4. Circular wait: A set of threads is waiting for each other in a circular chain.